ted it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In most cases,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Swift type system prevents a task group from escaping like that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because adding a child task to a task group is a mutating operation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and mutation operations can’t be performed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from a concurrent execution context like a child task.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Refer to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" documentation for detailed discussion of semantics shared between all task groups."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Discarding-behavior","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Discarding behavior"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A discarding task group eagerly discards and releases its child tasks as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"soon as they complete. This allows for the efficient releasing of memory used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by those tasks, which are not retained for future ","type":"text"},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" calls, as would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be the case with a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Cancellation behavior","anchor":"Cancellation-behavior","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A discarding task group becomes canceled in one of the following ways:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"when ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/cancelAll()"},{"text":" is invoked on it,","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"when the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" running this task group is canceled."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Since a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiscardingTaskGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a structured concurrency primitive, cancellation is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatically propagated through all of its child-tasks (and their child","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tasks).","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A canceled task group can still keep adding tasks, however they will start"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"being immediately canceled, and may act accordingly to this. To avoid adding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new tasks to an already canceled task group, use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/addTaskUnlessCancelled(priority:operation:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than the plain "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscardingTaskGroup\/addTask(priority:operation:)"},{"type":"text","text":" which adds tasks unconditionally."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For information about the language-level concurrency model that ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiscardingTaskGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is part of,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","type":"reference"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,